---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { api } from '../lib/api';
import { pct, usd } from '../lib/format';

const [meta, network, policyDoc] = await Promise.all([api.meta(), api.network(), api.policy()]);
const p = policyDoc?.policy;
const flows = [
  {
    n: '1', title: 'User signs in with a passkey',
    body: 'An OpenZeppelin smart account is created on Stellar; the passkey is the key. No seed phrase to lose, no extension to install.',
  },
  {
    n: '2', title: 'A vault is deployed for that user',
    body: 'The vault is a Soroban contract owned by the smart account. The backend proposes; it cannot move a cent.',
  },
  {
    n: '3', title: 'USDC arrives',
    body: 'From an existing wallet, from a SEP-24 anchor (KYC stays with the licensed anchor), or from another chain via CCTP — no bridge custodian.',
  },
  {
    n: '4', title: 'The keeper proposes, the vault decides',
    body: 'A permissionless keeper builds a plan. The vault checks it against the signed policy and against NAV before/after. A value-losing move reverts inside the same transaction.',
  },
];
const invariants = [
  'No arbitrary transfer entry point: the vault can only call registered adapters, and adapters only return funds to the vault.',
  'Rebalance is permissionless but policy-bounded and NAV-checked; automation cannot exceed what the user signed.',
  'The owner can always withdraw. Illiquid parts return as “pending” and are shown — never hidden.',
  'Keeper bounties are paid by the app treasury, never from user principal.',
  'Vaults are immutable by default; upgrading requires a new version and per-user opt-in migration.',
  'Freezing a venue blocks new deposits immediately while withdrawals stay open. Freezing is instant; unfreezing needs a timelock.',
];
---
<Base title="How it works" subtitle="Non-custodial, automatic, and boring in the places that matter: the parts that can move money are small, bounded and testable." network={network} meta={meta}>
  <div class="grid g4">
    {flows.map((f) => (
      <div class="card flow">
        <span class="n num">{f.n}</span>
        <h3>{f.title}</h3>
        <p class="small muted">{f.body}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="grid g2 stack">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Six invariants we test</h2>
      <ul class="inv">
        {invariants.map((i) => <li><span class="tick">✓</span><span>{i}</span></li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card" id="policy">
      <h2>The policy you sign</h2>
      {p ? (
        <div class="kv small">
          <div><span>Max in one venue</span><span class="num">{(p.max_venue_bps / 100).toFixed(0)}%</span></div>
          <div><span>Always liquid</span><span class="num">{(p.min_idle_bps / 100).toFixed(0)}%</span></div>
          <div><span>Max single move</span><span class="num">{(p.max_move_bps / 100).toFixed(0)}%</span></div>
          <div><span>Min. improvement to move</span><span class="num">{p.min_improvement_bps} bps</span></div>
          <div><span>Cooldown</span><span class="num">{p.cooldown_secs / 86400} days</span></div>
          <div><span>NAV tolerance</span><span class="num">{p.max_slippage_bps} bps</span></div>
          <div><span>Max venue utilisation</span><span class="num">{(p.max_venue_utilization_bps / 100).toFixed(0)}%</span></div>
          <div><span>Min. venue size</span><span class="num">{usd(p.min_capacity_usd)}</span></div>
          <div><span>Max share of a venue</span><span class="num">{(p.max_venue_share_of_capacity * 100).toFixed(0)}%</span></div>
        </div>
      ) : <p class="small muted">Policy unavailable.</p>}
      <p class="small muted mt">
        These values were chosen by measurement, not taste. The cooldown is two days because measured leadership
        between the verified venues lasts about a week; a seven-day cooldown missed most switches.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card stack">
    <h2>Architecture</h2>
    <pre class="arch mono">
passkey smart account (owner)
        │ owner auth
        ▼
   UserVault (one per user, immutable by default)
     ├── idle USDC sleeve          policy: min_idle_bps
     ├── positions per venue       policy: max_venue_bps, max_move_bps, cooldown
     └── rebalance(plan)           ANYONE → policy check → NAV check → revert on loss
             ├── BlendAdapter     supply / withdraw / position_value / liquidity_now
             └── DeFindexAdapter  deposit / withdraw / share_price / position_value

Registry (2/3 multisig + 48h timelock; guardian can freeze instantly)
Go backend:  venue ingestion · risk engine · policy planner · keeper log · read-only API
Astro:       server-rendered dashboard (no client key, no API token in the browser)</pre>
    <p class="small muted">
      The backend is deliberately the least powerful component. It reads the chain, scores venues and returns
      unsigned intents. There is no signing key in it, so compromising it does not move funds — the worst case is a
      bad proposal, which the vault rejects.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card stack callout">
    <h2>What we will not claim</h2>
    <ul class="no">
      <li>No fixed APY, no “beat inflation”, no principal protection. Yield comes from borrowers paying interest and can fall.</li>
      <li>Not “KYC-free”. The app takes no custody and performs no KYC; a fiat ramp means the licensed anchor performs KYC.</li>
      <li>We are not an aggregator while the venue count is small. We are a policy-driven allocator, and its value grows as decorrelated venues appear.</li>
      <li>A risk score cannot see a zero-day contract bug or an issuer freezing a balance. It prices what is observable and dated.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .flow { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
  .n { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--brand); }
  .flow h3 { margin: 0; }
  .stack { margin-top: 14px; }
  .inv { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: 13px; }
  .inv li { display: flex; gap: 9px; padding: 7px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #F3EBDB; color: #4A3D2C; }
  .inv li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .tick { color: var(--brand); font-weight: 700; flex: none; }
  .kv { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
  .kv div { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; border-bottom: 1px dashed #F3EBDB; padding: 5px 0; }
  .kv span:first-child { color: var(--muted); }
  .mt { margin-top: 12px; }
  .arch { background: #2E2418; color: #F3E9D8; padding: 16px; border-radius: 10px; overflow-x: auto; line-height: 1.45; font-size: 11.5px; }
  .callout { background: #FFFCF6; border-color: #E8DCC6; }
  .no { margin: 0 0 0 18px; padding: 0; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; color: #4A3D2C; }
</style>
